.TH LLAPI_MIRROR_FIND_STALE 3 2026-10-21 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_mirror_find_stale, llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags \- find stale components
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_mirror_find_stale(struct llapi_layout *" layout ,
.BI "                            struct llapi_resync_comp *" comp ,
.BI "                            size_t " comp_size ", __u16 *" mirror_ids ,
.BI "                            int " ids_nr );
.PP
.BI "int llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags(struct llapi_layout *" layout ,
.BI "                                  struct llapi_resync_comp *" comp ,
.BI "                                  size_t " comp_size ,
.BI "                                  __u16 *" mirror_ids ", int " ids_nr ,
.BI "                                  uint32_t " flags );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions collect the components of a mirrored (FLR) file
.I layout
that are marked stale
.RB ( LCME_FL_STALE ),
so that they can be resynced from an in-sync mirror.
For each component found, they fill one entry of the
.I comp
array of
.I comp_size
entries:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
struct llapi_resync_comp {
        uint64_t lrc_start;     /* start of the component extent */
        uint64_t lrc_end;       /* end of the component extent */
        uint32_t lrc_mirror_id; /* mirror id of the component */
        uint32_t lrc_id;        /* component id */
        bool     lrc_synced;    /* set to true here */
};
.EE
.in
.PP
If
.I ids_nr
is non-zero, only the components of the
.I ids_nr
mirrors listed in
.I mirror_ids
are collected. Otherwise the components of all mirrors are collected,
except those of mirrors marked
.BR LCME_FL_NOSYNC ,
unless
.I flags
has
.BR LCME_FL_NOSYNC .
.PP
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale ()
collects only data components, and never the parity components
.RB ( LCME_FL_PARITY )
of an Erasure Coded (EC) file. Use it when the caller writes file data
into the stale components itself, for example with
.BR llapi_mirror_copy_many ():
a parity component must not be written with file data.
.PP
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags ()
also collects the kinds of component given in
.IR flags ,
after the stale data components:
.TP
.B LCME_FL_PARITY
the stale parity components, including, with
.IR mirror_ids ,
those protecting the listed data mirrors.
.TP
.B LCME_FL_NOSYNC
with
.I ids_nr
of 0, also the stale components of mirrors marked
.BR LCME_FL_NOSYNC ,
and the parity components computed from them. Mirrors listed in
.I mirror_ids
are collected whether or not they are marked
.BR LCME_FL_NOSYNC .
.PP
With
.I flags
of 0 it is the same as
.BR llapi_mirror_find_stale ().
Use it with
.B LCME_FL_PARITY
and
.BR llapi_mirror_resync_many_params (3),
which copies the data components and then recomputes the parity
components. A file whose data mirror is in sync can still have stale
parity components, after a write to it.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Both functions return the number of components collected on success, or
a negative errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B -EINVAL
The components found do not fit in
.IR comp_size
entries, or
.I flags
has a flag other than
.B LCME_FL_PARITY
and
.BR LCME_FL_NOSYNC .
.PP
The errors of
.BR llapi_layout_comp_use (3)
are also returned if
.I layout
cannot be iterated.
.SH EXAMPLES
Find and resync all stale components of an open file
.IR fd ,
holding a resync lease:
.EX
        struct llapi_resync_comp comps[1024];
        struct llapi_layout *layout;
        uint64_t start, end;
        int count, i, rc;
\&
        layout = llapi_layout_get_by_fd(fd, 0);
        count = llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags(layout, comps,
                                              sizeof(comps) / sizeof(comps[0]),
                                              NULL, 0, LCME_FL_PARITY);
        if (count <= 0) {
                /* error, or nothing to resync */
                llapi_layout_free(layout);
                return count;
        }
\&
        start = comps[0].lrc_start;
        end = comps[0].lrc_end;
        for (i = 1; i < count; i++) {
                if (comps[i].lrc_start < start)
                        start = comps[i].lrc_start;
                if (comps[i].lrc_end > end)
                        end = comps[i].lrc_end;
        }
        rc = llapi_mirror_resync_many_params(fd, layout, comps, count,
                                             start, end, 0, 0);
        /* clear LCME_FL_STALE of each entry with lrc_synced set */
        llapi_layout_free(layout);
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_mirror_find_stale()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library since release 2.11.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_10_55_0-57-g79da3738df22
.B llapi_mirror_find_stale_flags()
is part of it since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_62-xxx-gxxxxxxxxxxx
